Patch 15 -- p71/p72 bridges: the clang-MS island, entry 41, and two witnesses.

Incremental after patch 14 and Wine patches 69-70.

Entry 39 gains the p71 bounded shader witness: one sample every 4,096 native
applications reads GL_CURRENT_PROGRAM, GL_PROGRAM_PIPELINE_BINDING and
GL_DRAW_FRAMEBUFFER_BINDING plus glGetError, and counts zero-program and
GL-error samples. That witness is what turned p71's black frame from "the
boundary does not work" into "nothing was bound, and here is the object that
explains why". Memory only, no stderr, no per-draw cost.

Entry 41 is the fused A+B+C root: one pointer to a guest-stack argument object,
no result, failing closed to the guest body when the TLS guard is unavailable.
Its p72 record counts applications and guest fallbacks; arming it is how a
non-diagnostic candidate build proves its route is live at all, since the
"entry matched" line exists only in the diagnostics build.

mgs2_ab_guest_capable() now lists entry 41 alongside 38 and 40, so the symmetric
guest-side selector works for the fused root with one registration path.

Build the island with clang for the MS layout, and regenerate the Class-B table
when doing so: clang inlines more, so the table is ~1,548 ids rather than GCC's
1,616, and a stale table would leave reachable slots without a native target.

